  "the-gentleman-from-san-francisco-and-other-stori": `Ivan Bunin’s 1915 stories, gathered as The Gentleman from San Francisco and Other Stories. Enter one room at a time.`,
  "the-getting-of-wisdom": `Four children on the grass: a prince, a golden crown, and a silk dress already dirty at the hem. School-status novel, not a children's book — Melbourne Ladies' College is the sit.`,
  "the-glimpses-of-the-moon": `A couple marries on other people’s houses and finds the bill. Sit with the world a moment before the first breath.`,
  "the-gods-are-athirst": `Anatole France’s 1912 novel The Gods Are Athirst. Sit with the world a moment before the first breath.`,
  "the-good-soldier": `This is the saddest story I have ever heard. Part I, Chapter I — the Ashburnhams and nine seasons at Nauheim. Skip the Contents. Ford Madox Ford’s 1915 novel.`,
  "the-great-god-pan": `A London experiment that lets something older into a girl’s nerves. Sit with the world a moment before the first breath.`,
  "the-greater-inclination": `The Greater Inclination (1899): New York manners, money, and the social misstep that becomes a life. Enter one room at a time.`,
  "the-green-carnation": `He slipped a green carnation into his evening coat and looked at himself in the Piccadilly glass — a Burne-Jones angel a little weary of its own life. Skip the credit block. Hichens’s 1894 novel. Coded desire stays as printed.`,
  "the-green-helmet-and-other-poems": `The Green Helmet and Other Poems (1910): Ireland, occult argument, and a tower that keeps the wind. Let the first line arrive when you are ready.`,
  "the-hand-of-ethelberta": `The Hand of Ethelberta (1876): Wessex parish weather, and a fate that looks like a neighbor. Sit with the world a moment before the first breath.`,
