  "the-poetic-edda": `Anonymous’s 1923 poems: The Poetic Edda. Let the first line arrive when you are ready.`,
  "the-professor": `The other day, in looking over my papers, I found in my desk the following copy of a letter, sent by me a year since to an old school acquaintance. Chapter I, Introductory — an Eton letter and Crimsworth the outsider. Skip the Preface and the Contents. Charlotte Brontë’s 1857 novel.`,
  "the-prophet": `Gibran’s Almustafa speaks on love, work, and leaving — counsel in a departing voice. Sit with the world a moment before the first breath.`,
